# APE fork provenance

Upstream: https://github.com/Attempto/APE
Fork base: 5f4d5354a45fb772763bf1a9543f508f15b28982
License: LGPL-3.0-or-later. The upstream `LICENSE.txt` is retained verbatim in this directory.

This tree is a liberal in-place fork: upstream files are edited directly,
first-party modules are added directly, and everything outside the compiler's
load and build closure is deleted. Git history against the fork base is the
complete change record. Every modified upstream file carries a prominent
dated in-file modification notice (GPL-3.0 §5(a) via LGPL-3.0-or-later);
first-party additions state their origin and license in their file header.

First-party additions:

- `prolog/ace_to_pl.pl` — ACE → plain-Prolog compiler over the APE parser
  (LGPL-3.0-or-later, APE derivative). Sole first-party entry point into this
  tree; contract in its header.

Trust posture: APE runs in separate SWI-Prolog processes over a scratch copy
staged by `tools/goal.py` (`shutil.copytree` + `fit_to_plp` grammar build);
Python moves bytes only and never interprets DRS content.
